// Branches 2 & 3: safety (detumbling and safe mode).

structure detumble_ok #safety {
    ```
    From both post-separation and FDIR re-entry conditions, the satellite completes detumbling and reaches safe mode without external intervention
    ```
    children:
        detumble_convergence_ok,
        mtq_authority_ok,
        rate_sensor_available
}

bind detumble_convergence_ok {
    ```
    Starting from the maximum tip-off rate {$max_tipoff_rate}, B-dot control damps the body rate to a safe-mode-transition level within {$detumble_time_limit}
    ```
    veriq: "aocs.verify_detumble"
}

fiat mtq_authority_ok {
    ```
    The magnetorquer dipole moment provides sufficient control torque for B-dot control across the geomagnetic field strengths of the target orbit ({$orbit_altitude})
    ```
    until: FM
    promote: bind
}

fiat rate_sensor_available {
    ```
    The rate information required for detumbling remains available under gyro failure, from redundant sensing including estimation with coarse sun sensors and magnetometers
    ```
}

structure safe_mode_ok #safety {
    ```
    In safe mode, the satellite maintains, without external intervention, a state satisfying all of the following:

    - The angle between the solar-array normal and the sun direction stays within {$safemode_sun_angle} (positive power balance)
    - Mode transition completes within {$safemode_entry_time} of anomaly detection
    - All mission equipment is off and every unit stays within its thermal safety range
    ```
    children:
        sun_pointing_stable,
        fdir_transition_ok,
        safemode_power_positive
}

bind sun_pointing_stable {
    ```
    Safe-mode sun pointing acquires the sun starting from the residual rates left after detumbling, and thereafter keeps the sun angle within {$safemode_sun_angle}
    ```
    veriq: "aocs.verify_sun_pointing"
}

fiat fdir_transition_ok {
    ```
    The detection conditions and transition sequence for attitude anomalies (rate exceedance, loss of attitude determination, wheel failure) guarantee safe-mode arrival within {$safemode_entry_time} of detection
    ```
    until: FM
    promote: bind
}

// Ideally shared with a power-domain argument; kept local in this
// single-domain example (see README on namespaces).
fiat safemode_power_positive {
    ```
    In the safe-mode configuration (all mission equipment off, sun angle within {$safemode_sun_angle}), generated power exceeds the configuration's consumption under all orbit conditions including eclipse
    ```
}
